# Rust build output — fully reproducible.
# No leading slash: it has to catch nested targets like spikes/*/target too.
# `/target/` would only match the root.
target/

# MSVC debug symbols
*.pdb

# Editors / IDEs
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Personal working notes — kept local, never committed.
KARAR.md
KARARLAR.md
research/

# Cargo.lock is committed ON PURPOSE: kubide is an application, not a library.
# Pinning versions is what makes the same commit still build months later,
# which matters most with fast-moving dependencies like windows-rs.
